		{"id":"ef7635ffbae6f372","type":"text","text":" **HAS CROSS REFERENCE are generated by using the primary key referencing tables.**\n\n1. Process 1 metadata inference remain as it is.\n2. In process 2 while generating the relationships we need to lookup with the things\n\t1. We are not using foreign key referencing tables for creating the cross reference\n\t2. we are generating the edges using the field primary key referencing table.\n\t3. Keep the logic of generating the  foreign key referencing tables same\n3. In process 3 separate the logic of **HAS_CROSS_REFERENCE** (table to table relationship)","x":-520,"y":-260,"width":920,"height":460},
		{"id":"5af38f78ad630be0","type":"text","text":"**HAS_CROSS_REFERENCE relationships are generated using primary key–referencing tables.**\n\n1. **Process 1:** Keep metadata inference unchanged.\n    \n2. **Process 2:** While generating relationships, follow these rules:\n    \n    - we are not using foreign key–referencing tables for creating cross references.\n        \n    - Instead, generating edges based on primary key–referencing tables.\n        \n    - Keep the existing logic for generating foreign key–based relationships unchanged.\n\n\t* make updates related to primary key referencing tables.\n        \n3. **Process 3:** Separate the logic for handling **HAS_CROSS_REFERENCE** (table-to-table relationships).","x":-359,"y":760,"width":999,"height":340}
